    },
    {
      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "content": "<p>Using an approach inspired by Chinese ink painting, Nakabayashi Chikutō painted these rocky cliffs out of stacked cubes that contrast with the sinewy tree trunks. At the lower right, a scholar makes his way up to the building in the center: the perfect place from which to view the waterfall nearby.</p>\n<p>Chikutō was born in Nagoya. At a pivotal moment in his career, he came under the patronage of a wealthy merchant named Kamiya Tenyū, a collector of Chinese paintings. Throughout his life, Chikutō maintained that copying the Chinese masters was the most effective way to learn the art of painting.</p>\n",
